<title>SWEDEN: FORECAST-MoDo '96 profit seen lower.</title>
<headline>FORECAST-MoDo '96 profit seen lower.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Analysts expect Swedish forestry company MoDo to post a 3.06 billion crown profit after financial items for 1996, a poll showed on Thursday.</p>
<p>In 1995 MoDo posted a profit of 5.22 billion crowns.</p>
<p>Forecasts from 14 analysts ranged from 2.91 billion crowns to 3.27 billion.</p>
<p>For 1997, analysts on average expect the company to report a profit of 1.78 billion crowns.</p>
<p>The dividend is expected to be 7.8 crowns per share, the poll showed.</p>
<p>MoDo is due to publish its 1996 result on February 19.</p>
<p>Analysts who participated in the survey were from James Capel, Paribas, Kleinwort Benson, Swedbank, Fiba Nordic, Fischer Partners, Morgan Grenfell, Nordbanken, Enskilda, Handelsbanken, Aragon, Ohman, Goldman Sachs and Aros.</p>
<p> (Millions of crowns)   AVG	  RANGE     ANALYSTS</p>
<p>Profit after fin items</p>
<p>	    1996	     3,056   2,912-3,266    14</p>
<p>	    1997	     1,779     779-2,488    14</p>
<p>	    1998	     2,798     898-4,480    12</p>
<p> Profit/shr 1996 (crowns)   24	23-25.9     9</p>
<p> Dividend (crowns)	  7.80    4.30-9.00    12</p>
<p>-- Olle Lindstrom, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1015</p>
